# Sonarr and Radarr API keys — one logical secret, six variables, four
# consumers. Copy to secrets/arr-keys.env, fill in, then
# `./scripts/secrets encrypt`.
#
# Generate each key yourself (any 32-char hex string works):
#   openssl rand -hex 16
#
# THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH, not a copy of what the apps
# generated. Sonarr and Radarr are *told* their key via the Servarr
# environment override (APP__SECTION__KEY), so a deploy onto empty config
# directories comes up with the keys already wired into recyclarr and
# unpackerr, instead of generating random ones and silently breaking both.
#
# The duplicated values are deliberate: each tool expects its own
# spelling, and keeping them in one file means rotation is a single edit
# rather than three. These four services are one trust domain — unlike
# the VPN key, which stays in its own file precisely because gluetun is
# not in that domain.
#
# To rotate: change the value everywhere it appears below, encrypt, then
# `docker compose up -d sonarr radarr recyclarr unpackerr`. The apps will
# adopt the new key on start; nothing needs touching in their UIs.

# --- consumed by the apps themselves (Servarr env override) ---
SONARR__AUTH__APIKEY=
RADARR__AUTH__APIKEY=

# --- consumed by recyclarr, via !env_var in recyclarr/recyclarr.yml ---
# Same values as above.
SONARR_API_KEY=
RADARR_API_KEY=

# --- consumed by unpackerr ---
# Same values again.
UN_SONARR_0_API_KEY=
UN_RADARR_0_API_KEY=
